    "notes": "Paired independent ways361503808 and361503809 identify the entrance to Yasnaya Polyana. Retained mapped centers are5.229m apart along northeast/southwest; X northeast across the pair, Z southeast toward the outside approach, baked native axes with heading0 at the unchanged assigned collection anchor in the passage. Outside and inside photos establish green bell roofs, white cylinders and estate-facing northwest arched doors. PMTiles envelopes are broad relative to the photographed spacing: preserve both centers/ownership outlines while using photo-led slim bodies at60% of equivalent map radius, about1.8..1.92m diameter. This is an explicit map/photo reconciliation, not an exact surveyed footprint. Wing walls extend only outward, preserving the passage. Retained Protomaps20261020 and Mapzen201x201/6m ground; passage provider[0,0] supplies202.90528695999353m datum. Boundary grades-0.279..0.222m; northeast base+.05m/foundation-.5m and southwest base+.3m/foundation-.2m. Original ground remains between and around both towers. Only actual slim circular feet and two outward wing-wall feet cut it; never bridge their masks across the road. Coarse ground leaves some exposed plinth and unequal bases. No flattening or bespoke survey; independent neighbors, roads and ponds remain. Two owned map records replaced,241 resident/293 wider independent buildings retained. All original roads, passage ground and40070.675m² pond water remain. Actual model feet and outward walls alone cut the ground; the two circular masks remain separate. Failure retains all243 originals; every LOD/failure/unload restores ground/water with zero live model geometry. Three explicit passage probes and all outside approaches retain their original terrain. Mesh checks establish more than3m clear between the bodies."
