  "fidelityReview": {
    "target": "medium-fi",
    "status": "passed",
    "notes": "Both entrance gate towers as one geographically anchored ensemble: slim white round masonry bodies, low plinths, projecting circular cornices, curved green bell roofs, small finial vanes, physically recessed blind arched panels and arched green wooden doors on the estate side. Two short attached low white wing walls complete the historic exterior interpretation. The central entrance and original road ground stay open. Temporary visitor barriers, signs, people and interiors are omitted; exact door/wing inventory, levels and roof seam details remain reconstructed. No photograph pixels or inscription artwork copied. Photo-led approximate dimensions: white body3.05m above individual base, stepped cornice to3.23m, bell roof to4.24m and finial/vane to4.76m. Door opening.7m wide with1.95m spring and2.3m arched top; blind niches use a similar arch. Individual model radii.895/.962m derive from60% of equivalent cartographic radii; hidden seams, door hardware, absolute vertical scale and historical levels remain approximate. Retained Protomaps20261020 and Mapzen201x201/6m ground; passage provider[0,0] supplies202.90528695999353m datum. Boundary grades-0.279..0.222m; northeast base+.05m/foundation-.5m and southwest base+.3m/foundation-.2m. Original ground remains between and around both towers. Only actual slim circular feet and two outward wing-wall feet cut it; never bridge their masks across the road. Coarse ground leaves some exposed plinth and unequal bases. No flattening or bespoke survey; independent neighbors, roads and ponds remain. Ordinary outside/inside photographs establish the architecture and estate-facing doors. Map centers/ownership stay fixed; slimmer photo-led bodies reconcile broad cartographic envelopes with photographed spacing. That width reconciliation and the unsurveyed vertical scale are explicit approximations. Low wing extents, historical levels, threshold accessibility, seam count and vane direction remain reconstructed. Modern visitor barriers/signs and interior use are omitted. Native roads approach slightly asymmetrically and coarse ground partly hides the threshold/plinth; their source geometry is preserved. Other estate buildings remain procedural context in the isolated fixture. Physical phone/laptop measurements remain pending."
